# STATUS: DRAFT -- the CSR RTL change (Stage 2b csr_unit.vhd fp_csr sticky
#   accumulate) does not exist in this worktree (base 26e3980). Written against
#   the FROZEN design in x4_stage1_proposal.md §6 ("FP-op completion ORs the
#   op's flags into fp_csr[4:0] (sticky)"). Stage 3 finalizes the hunk
#   offset/context against the real csr_unit.vhd.
#
# WHAT IT MUTATES:
#   Target file      : hdl/common/vesta/csr_unit.vhd  (Stage 2b)
#   Design construct : the sticky fflags ACCUMULATE on fp_flags_we (proposal
#                      §6). The architected behavior ORs the op's flags into the
#                      held fflags so exceptions across a sequence accumulate.
#                      The seed replaces the OR with a plain assignment, so each
#                      op CLEARS the previous flags and only the LAST op's flags
#                      survive.
#
# DETECTING TEST : rv32uzf-p-daccum  (tools/gen_directed.py :: gen_daccum)
#   daccum clears fflags ONCE, then runs a sequence: fadd(NX), fdiv/0(DZ),
#   inf-inf(NV), overflow(OF|NX), underflow(UF|NX), and reads fflags ONCE at the
#   end expecting the OR = 0x1f. With the seed (assign not OR) only the last
#   op's flags remain (UF|NX = 0x03), so `bne s6,a5,fail` fires --> BOUNDED FAIL
#   (a0=0xDEADBEEF). Compare-and-branch, so a wrong value cannot hang the test.
#
# EXPECTED:  clean csr_unit.vhd -> rv32uzf-p-daccum = TEST PASSED  (fflags=0x1f)
#            seeded csr_unit.vhd -> rv32uzf-p-daccum = TEST FAILED  (fflags=0x03)
# =========================================================================
#
# STAGE-3 FINALIZED (2026-07-18) against the real Stage-2b csr_unit.vhd. The
#   sticky-OR lives at the fp_flags_we commit (guarded by ENABLE_ZFINX); the
#   seed replaces the OR with a plain assign (mutation semantics unchanged).
#   Applies cleanly to the merged tree; detecting test rv32uzf-p-daccum unchanged.
